NVMesh make file will make the test prgram if the 
build_sh_conf
include somethings as follows:
REMOTE_SERVERS+="n174:IM_TEST_DC=yes:MK_RPM=no "
REMOTE_SERVERS+="n224:IM_TEST_DC=yes:MK_RPM=no "

After the build there will be two modules:
1. dcc.ko - which is the client side module
2. dcs.ko - which is the server side module

There will /proc entries on both client and server
1. /proc/dc_test/dc_test_c - client
2. /proc/dc_test/dc_test_s - server

To test the modules start with the server by echoing the following:

From the server module directory:
cd ~/projects/dc_testing/testing/dc; sudo insmod dcs.ko; sudo bash -c 'echo 10.1.2.174:4321 > /proc/dc_test/dc_test_s'
The IP is the NIC we wish to use use and the port is not necessary but can be kept

From the server module directory:
cd ~/projects/dc_testing/testing/dc/; sudo insmod dcc.ko; sudo bash -c 'echo 10.1.2.224,10.1.2.174:4321 > /proc/dc_test/dc_test_c'
The first IP is the local IP we wish to bind and the second IP:PORT is the server side
  
The server can run using unmodified OFED code
The client MUST use a modified OFED - the one on n224  


